B6 fixes of 13 Nov 2026 (tracker: the two issues of 13 Nov), checked on Verilator 5.020
=====================================================================================

1. U11 hung on xsim 2024.2 (R-1111-01: banner, then nothing for 37 h)
   Cause   sched_pkg::epoch_len computed longint'(n_slots(n)) * frame_len(...) and
           doubled e while e < r. As a constant function at elaboration (the RTL's
           use) it is right; U11 also calls it at run time, where xsim misreads a
           cast of a call inside an expression (README rule 9), so the loop never
           ended. The restart then failed (XSIM 43-3356) because the hung xsimk.exe
           still held xsim.dir/tb_phase_sequencer_snap.
   Fix     rtl/pkg/sched_pkg.sv     epoch_len: casts into plain variables, a doubling
                                    loop of fixed bound (40 steps); same values
           tb/unit/tb_phase_sequencer.sv   casts into variables before use
           tb/common/sched_ref.sv   frame_ref.sample() and at(): casts into variables;
                                    at()'s cursor loop bounded and broken off early
                                    (each call O(1) again: U11 3 s instead of 23 s)

2. Same-edge races in the mesh bench (counts differed by simulator; every run passed)
   TL05    reset released by a blocking assignment at a falling edge, where the
           always @(negedge clk) comparison tests rst_n: Verilator ran the bench
           first and compared once more (500,650 / 146,658 / 7,545,943 against
           xsim's and Riviera-PRO's 500,649 / 146,657 / 7,545,942)
   TL04    $finish at a falling edge: Riviera-PRO ran that edge's negedge checkers
           first (EDA bundle 246,084 against Verilator's 246,013)
   Fix     tb/mesh/mesh_bench.sv    g_shadow: sh_on <= rst_n at the rising edge,
                                    compare only when sh_on; designs C and D finish
                                    on a rising edge
           README rule 10 (Section 2), D53

